## RISE
Net sales rose 11% to $1.24 billion in fiscal 2025, led by 19% growth in cordless power tools, and gross margin improved to 38.5% as steel and freight costs eased [1]. First-quarter fiscal 2026 sales grew 7% to $301 million, while inventory rose to $412 million as the company stocked its new Monterrey plant [1][2]. Its three largest retail customers make up 46% of net sales [1]. In June it recalled about 40,000 cordless drills over battery overheating, at an estimated cost of $9 million to $12 million [3].

## FLAT
Revenue was flat at $3.05 billion in fiscal 2025, as 4% price increases offset a 4% volume decline, and operating margin fell to 9.1% on higher wheat and packaging costs [4]. Chief operating officer Dana Ruiz became chief executive on June 1, 2026, succeeding Lee Park [5]. The company plans to close two bakeries by early 2027, expecting $35 million in yearly savings after about $50 million in one-time costs, affecting about 420 jobs [6].
